==Battleground==
*7 [[Trolly Blogger]]s (100%) spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
*7 [[Trolly Blogger]]s (100%) spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Riceball Cat (Enemy)|Riceball Cat]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Trolly Blogger]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s (100%) spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Riceball Cat (Enemy)|Riceball Cat]] spawns.
**30 [[Riceball Cat (Enemy)|Riceball Cats]] spawn, delay 3~6 seconds<sup>90f~180f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Riceball Cat (Enemy)|Riceball Cats]] spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This level can be easily beaten with Meatshields. [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]]; or something similar. Basically the standard meatshield + midranger + big backliner army.

When the first [[Trolly Blogger]] appears, start saving up money and buy a Paris Cat. When you see the first [[Riceball Cat (Enemy)|Riceball Cat]] getting near the [[Cat Base]], start spamming Crazed Wall Cat and Eraser Cat along with Paris, Dragon and Ururun. Stop when the situation degenerates.

When there are 5-8 Riceball Cats on the battlefield, start spamming your other meatshields, Jamiera and Bahamut.

Keep up with this and you should win the level. Also, be sure to bring a [[Treasure Radar]] (only if you're sure of winning) to have a 100% chance of unlocking the [[True Form]] for [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Sumo Cat]]. If you are confident that you can beat [[Oh Yokozuna! (Insane)|the second level]], then do not bring a Treasure Radar.

